# DA-Bench id 361: count |z|>3 outliers in wind speed, weather_train.csv (16683 rows). #
# NOT in test.sh: label says 0, our (correct) answer is 97 -- a label discrepancy. #
# We compute "how many outliers are there" = values with |z|>3 = 97 (pandas and #
# numpy agree, with both sample and population std). The prompt also says "remove #
# the outliers and create a new dataframe", and the reference apparently reported #
# the outlier count OF THAT cleaned dataframe, which is 0 by construction (you just #
# removed them). So the label measures outliers-remaining-after-removal, not the #
# count of outliers. Emitting 0 would be tautological, so we keep the honest 97. #
let data = ^^csv("weather_train.csv") in
count_z_out(num(data.`wind speed`), 3.0)
